  "response": "The solution has been written to `/work/answer.md`.\n\n### Summary of Results\nFor a non-degenerate polygon $F$ ($v_P > 0$, $v_A, v_B, v_C > 0$, $v_A + v_B + v_C > v_P$), the Vickrey-nearest core point $p^{\\text{VN}}$ equals the centroid of $F$ **if and only if** at least one of the following three conditions holds:\n1. **No value cap binds on $F$:** $v_A \\ge v_P$, $v_B \\ge v_P$, and $v_C \\ge v_P$ ($F$ is the simplex triangle).\n2. **No zero-payment floor binds on $F$:** $v_A + v_B \\le v_P$, $v_B + v_C \\le v_P$, and $v_C + v_A \\le v_P$ ($F$ is an inverted equilateral triangle, even when $v_A, v_B, v_C$ are distinct).\n3. **Full winner symmetry:** $v_A = v_B = v_C$ ($F$ is a regular hexagon or equilateral triangle).",
